{% comment %}
  The one description string, for both the meta description and the social
  cards.

  Usage:
    {%- capture meta_description -%}{%- render 'suf-meta-description' -%}{%- endcapture -%}

  ONE SNIPPET BECAUSE TWO PLACES CONSUME IT. snippets/SEO-tags.liquid and
  snippets/social-meta-tags.liquid both need it, and a page whose search result
  and whose shared link describe it differently is worse than either alone.

  The chain, best source first:

    page_description        the page's own Search engine listing -> Description,
                            per page, in admin. Nothing in the repo can set it.
    shop.description        Online Store -> Preferences -> meta description.
                            One string for the whole store.
    the theme setting       a floor, so nothing ever renders bare.

  A SITE-WIDE DEFAULT IS A FLOOR, NOT A TARGET. Search engines treat one
  description repeated across every page as no description at all, and usually
  write their own from the page copy instead. What it does buy is the social
  card: a link shared to Slack or iMessage falls back to this rather than to
  the shop name, and that is where a bare tag looks worst. Fill in the per-page
  field wherever the page matters.

  Keep it under about 155 characters. Longer is truncated mid-sentence in a
  result, which reads worse than a short one.
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign d = page_description
  if d == blank
    assign d = shop.description
  endif
  if d == blank
    assign d = settings.suf_seo_description
  endif
  echo d | strip_newlines | strip
-%}
